# Intentionally unimplemented.
#
# Indexing currently runs inline in the API process (lumora/api/routes/index.py
# offloads the blocking clone/parse/embed pipeline with asyncio.to_thread), so a
# separate worker container would have no queue to consume. Celery and redis are
# declared in pyproject.toml but nothing dispatches to them yet.
#
# Split this out when indexing needs to outlive a request: add a broker service
# to docker-compose.yml, move _run_indexing behind a Celery task, and build this
# stage from the same base as docker/Dockerfile.api with a celery worker CMD.
